    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh! Hey <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span>!”</span> It’s <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Manuel</span>, walking over with a big smile, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I see you’ve met <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>. Remember? He’s the one I told you about. The one who knows about the…”</span> He nudges <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span> twice, <span style="color:Pink">probably referring to your knowledge of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Manuel</span>’s little cage.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“O- Oh! H- hi there. I’m <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span>.”</span> The boy introduces himself, seeming a bit calmer since you are <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Manuel</span>’s friend. <span style="color:Pink">You figure it would be weird for you to mention his own cage, since you’re not supposed to know about that,</span> so simply smile and introduce yourself as well. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry about bumping into you. I- I felt a pinch and slipped and…”</span> The boy freezes, <span style="color:Pink">realizing he said too much and quickly looks down still blushing.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span> is a little shy, but he’s super cool.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Manuel</span> happily puts his arm around the quiet boy, smiling. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I actually just met him recently. Turns out we have a lot in common.”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You figure he is implying about the cages again, but refrain from bringing up your knowledge about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span>’, to prevent the shy boy from getting more embarrassed.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“We’ve got a lot of classes together too! Hey, the two of you should hang out sometime. I’m sure you’d get along great!”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I- I-<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“ <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span> stutters out, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’m okay with that… if- if he wants to.”</span> He gives you a nervous smile. You return his smile and nod; you’d love to hang out with and get to know him. <span style="color:Pink">Though whether that is out of a desire to have another friend or learn more about his tiny cage and that strange underwear he is wearing is your business.</span> With that, both boys return to their seats, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span> seeming a little less stressed now that he’s maybe made another friend. <br>
