    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I… I…”</span> <span style="color:Pink">The boy looks like he is about to explode in embarrassment, turning redder and redder.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I got to go!”</span> He quickly spins around, running towards the door even though class is still in session. Not wanting an awkward moment that will turn everyone’s attention to you, you quickly stop him by grabbing him by the arm. <br>
    <br>
    You apologize to the boy if you made him nervous. You introduce yourself and tell him he has no need to be scared, you don’t bite. <span style="color:LightGreen">Your smile and kind words seem to calm him down a little, though he still seems very shy.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I- I- I’m <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Enkys</span>. N- Nice to meet you.”</span> He stutters out, staring at his feet. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry again.”</span> You tell him it’s no problem, nothing broke and no one was injured, so it’s all good!
    
